  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "We learn about the passion for cooking that started in childhood and led to military kitchen duty. Celebrity restaurant owner Dmitry Nagiyev visits the mess hall, tastes the soup, and offers an incredible opportunity. Listen to the story in Russian first, and then we will examine every line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я всегда знала, что буду поваром.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не пожарным и не космонавтом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Даже не президентом. А именно поваром.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Вот он, наш герой!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Мне очень понравилась ваша солянка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо! Я очень старалась.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Молодец. Из ничего практически шедевр.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Хотите поработать в хорошем ресторане?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Конечно! Это моя мечта.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Милости просим. Буду рад.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Я говорю совершенно серьёзно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "В каком ресторане?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Ресторан Клод Моне в Москве.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо огромное! Я обязательно приду.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let's examine how a simple army soup opened the door to Moscow's culinary elite.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я всегда знала, что буду поваром.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I always knew I would be a chef.' The first words mean 'I always knew', followed by 'that I will be a chef' using the instrumental case.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не пожарным и не космонавтом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not a firefighter and not an astronaut.' Negative particles are repeated before each profession in the instrumental case.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Даже не президентом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not even president.' The word at the start means 'even', adding emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А именно поваром.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Specifically a chef.' The contrastive conjunction is paired with an adverb meaning 'namely' or 'precisely'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Вот он, наш герой!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here he is, our hero!' A proud exclamation introducing the talented cook.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Мне очень понравилась ваша солянка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I really liked your solyanka.' The past-tense verb agrees with the feminine noun for the traditional sour soup.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо! Я очень старалась.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you! I tried very hard.' A grateful reply using the past tense feminine form of the verb 'to try'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well done.' Nagiyev delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'well done'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Из ничего практически шедевр.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Practically a masterpiece out of nothing.' High praise from the celebrity guest, noting how great food can be made from basic ingredients.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Хотите поработать в хорошем ресторане?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Would you like to work in a good restaurant?' An invitation framed politely as a question about what the cook wants to do.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Конечно! Это моя мечта.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Of course! That is my dream.' A passionate response using the common word for 'dream'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Милости просим. Буду рад.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are welcome. I will be glad.' A warm traditional Russian formula of hospitality followed by a promise of being delighted to see them.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Я говорю совершенно серьёзно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am speaking completely seriously.' Nagiyev chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'speak' for the ongoing action, followed by 'completely' and 'seriously'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dmitry",
      "t": "Ресторан Клод Моне в Москве.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Restaurant Claude Monet in Moscow.' Nagiyev delivers a punchy one-word reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'restaurant'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо огромное! Я обязательно приду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you very much! I will definitely come.' An enthusiastic promise using the adverb for 'definitely'. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
